<Base title="About Alex Janiak" description="Alex Janiak is cofounder and Chief Scientist of Pareto Inference and writes about LLM inference optimization, GPU systems, forecasting, and mechanism design.">
	<h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

	<img class="about-photo" src="/alex-janiak.jpg" alt="Alex Janiak" width="400" height="400" />

	<p><span class="newthought">Hi! I'm <span class="accent">Alex Janiak</span></span>. I'm cofounder &amp; Chief Scientist of <a href="https://paretoinference.com">Pareto Inference</a>, where I tune custom and open-source model inference. I want a world where intelligence is open and abundant, so I'm starting with making it dirt cheap.</p>

	<p>I'm also a systems freak, so most of what I write here now is technical: how to make LLM inference fast and cheap, from kernels and batching to caching, quantization, and the systems that hold it all together.</p>

	<p>Older posts are about decision theory, forecasting, prediction markets, and mechanism design.</p>

